            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I served this dip with fritos scoops to some picky guests, and everyone loved it! I added a heaping half teaspoon each of garlic salt and cumin after reading reviews about it being bland. Instead of mexicorn I used frozen corn and chopped my own green and red bell pepper- half of each. I also added some fresh cilantro in the mix and for garnish. It turned out great and before I knew it the bowl was empty!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I only had two cans of Mexi-corn on hand so that's all I could add and because I was making this a hot dip, I used reduced fat cream cheese instead of mayonnaise. I didn't add the extra jalapeno pepper because I had small kids eating this dip so I omitted it. I threw all the ingredients for this into my small crockpot after breakfast and set it to cook until lunch time. We really liked this. Next time I make this, I might cut back on the sour cream just a bit and maybe add a little salsa. GREAT with tortilla chips. I've had this before cold but I think making it hot was just as good. Good quick dip for our weekend snack day made with on hand ingredients on the cheap.",
            "datePublished": "2011-01-23T11:59:25.283Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "susanctr"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for the first time and took to a family party. My little grandson loved it and everyone else liked it too. I added the heaping 1/2 teaspoon of garlic salt and cumin. It still needed some flavoring so I added a dash of salt and some black pepper and that helped. Didn't think 8 ounces of sour cream was enough so I added 16 ounces to hold the dip together. Would add one more pepper next time and a few more green onions. Blended the pepper and onions in a food processor with a little water so they wouldn't be chuncky.",
            "datePublished": "2010-12-12T20:20:55.030Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "hothilary36"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Not really that good as written, good base. I used one block cream cheese and skipped the mayo, placed in food processor, blend cheese and chilis and half of corn until chunky, place in bowl mix in remainder of corn and green onions. I also added garlic, and cumin to mine. Great with corn chips.",
            "datePublished": "2010-07-04T09:07:10.553Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I absolutely loveee this recipe. I got it from my mom a few years ago and it's a hit at every party I bring it to. I add more jalapenos and an extra can of green chilies. Then serve it with Fritos Scoops potato chips!!!",
            "datePublished": "2002-07-26T09:24:00.873Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Absolutely delicious!!!! It was incredibly easy to make. Definitely cut back on the onions next time. I didn't have any Mexican corn in the pantry so I used regular corn and added diced red bell peppers...PERFECT!",
            "datePublished": "2002-05-24T00:00:24.623Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Captain Awesome"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Added some crushed red pepper. Really set it off. Second time I made it only had 2 cans of corn so I used 1 can of black beans and actually liked it better. One of those basic recipes that takes kindly to creativity.",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-30T15:58:41.458Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Paige"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe rocks. I do not add jalapenos just because of personal preference. I do take extra time to roast the corn with some butter or oil, paprika, and sea salt. If you are doubling or tripling this recipe, roasting the corn is going to take about an hour, but it is so worth it. It gives the dip some extra flavor and depth.",
            "datePublished": "2020-05-17T17:14:23.560Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Soup Loving Nicole"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was easy to make and turned out pretty good. One thing to point out is that the directions didn't call for draining the corn. Two cans in and I could tell that I had too much liquid. I recommend draining the corn. It definitely needed salt too. I think it could have used a punch of acid as well so next time I will add some lime juice. Overall good recipe, easy to make, and one I would make again with some minor adjustments.",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-28T13:27:02.281Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Steph"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Our family loves this dip! I followed the recipe then added an extra can of the diced green chiles, a heaping 1/2 tsp of cumin and garlic salt. Green Giant Mexicorn is my corn choice.",
            "datePublished": "2024-06-11T17:45:00.444Z"
          },
